    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/media-arts-video-and-film-production-full-time-lecturer-faculty-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states-d7a6838a-47ce-4c2a-beba-e56d877b4279": {
      "title": "Media Arts (Video and Film Production), Full-Time Lecturer, Faculty",
      "description": "Media Arts (Video and Film Production), Full-Time Lecturer, Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Media Arts (Video and Film Production), Full-Time Lecturer, Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Media Arts (Video and Film Production), Full-Time Lecturer, Faculty 498688 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Media and Entertainment Lecturer Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Media Arts (Video and Film Production), Full-Time Lecturer, Faculty Department Media Arts University Expectation MTSU seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching and meaningful service. We also seek to attract culturally and academically diverse faculty who value working with diverse students. Salary The salary is commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Media Arts at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, temporary (non-tenurable) faculty position (#144020) in video and film production at the rank of lecturer. This is a one-year temporary appointment. The contract may be renewed annually based on available funding, demonstrated need, and satisfactory performance as assessed by annual evaluations. The start date for the appointment is January 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach a wide range of video and film production courses, including, but not limited to, preproduction, production, and postproduction, as well as aesthetics, history, and theory. Required Education A master's degree in video and film production or a closely related field is required by the appointment date. A bachelor's degree with three (3) years of full-time or six (6) years of part-time verifiable professional experience will be considered in lieu of a master's degree. In lieu of a master's or bachelor's degree, ten (10) years of full-time or twenty (20) years of part-time verifiable professional experience will be considered. Professional experience must be in cinematography, filmmaking, TV/film production, directing, editing, technical direction, or production executive roles. Other Desirables Applicants who include evidence in their application materials of instructional experience, such as conducting professional seminars, chairing presentations, or offering tutorials in areas relevant to the courses they will teach, will receive special consideration. In addition, applicants who include relevant awards, industry memberships, or certifications in creative/technical areas in their application materials will receive special consideration. Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and statement of creative activities as separate attachments when submitting the application. NOTE: The statement of creative activities must include the following: Chronological list of projects and the position(s) held. A link to an updated IMDB is preferred. List of links to representative samples of professional work. Special Instruction to Applicants If you need help with the application, please contact Mitzi Dunkley, Faculty Recruitment Specialist, at (615) 898-5128. If you have position-specific questions, please contact Jerod Hollyfield at Jerod.Hollyfield@mtsu.edu. MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee, their spouse, and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: 10/06/2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 463d56ac Last Name (required) ad475e6a Email (required) be308805 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administrative Assistant 3 - Tennessee Livestock Center Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, Other Responsible for all department office work, including but not limited to, budget reconciliation and revisions; composition of all correspondence and memorandum, payment authorizations, purchase orders, and payroll paperwork; preparation of legal contracts and department statements; completion of department timesheets; answering telephone and greeting visitors. Associate Athletic Trainer Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching The Associate Athletic Trainer will report to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine. The position will supervise and coordinate athletic training services for student-athletes in intercollegiate athletic programs – primarily men’s basketball. Essential duties include but are not be limited to: assist with the prevention, treatment, rehabilitation, physician referral, and medical documentation of all injuries associated with assigned student athletes; communicate with coaches, student athletes, parents, staff and physicians within NATA and HIPAA guidelines; observe all athletic policy and procedures in accordance with NATA regulations as well as NCAA, Conference USA and MTSU rules and remain certified to perform these duties on a daily basis. Coordinate Concussion testing and baseline testing for all assigned student athletes; provide supervision of daily practice and game coverage, in season travel, and summer sports workout coverage for assigned student athletes as permitted by NCAA legislation. Required to be flexible and adapt to schedule changes as necessary. Serve as an approved preceptor within the CAATE accredited graduate athletic training program. Provide direct supervision of intern athletic trainers for assigned sports and graduate athletic training students in the athletic training education program; instruct these students in professional prevention, care and rehabilitation of assigned student-athletes as well as the certification and licensure process. Required to attend national NATA and Conference USA meetings and/or conventions to remain current in their field for changes that occur. Assistant Director - Event Operations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Event Coordination Under the direction of the Associate Athletic Director for Capital Projects, assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of home athletic events across MTSU's 17 NCAA Division I sports and support daily operations of Athletics facilities. Serve as the primary on-site event manager for assigned sports and events; coordinate logistics with visiting teams, game officials, Athletics units, campus departments, contracted vendors, and public safety; support special events and external facility use; assist with operational planning for Athletics capital projects, including the renovation of Floyd Stadium; maintain Athletics inventory records; and assist with hiring, training, and supervising graduate assistants, student workers, and event staff. Night, weekend, and holiday work is required. Sign up for 