    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/chair-philosophy-and-religious-studies-tenure-track-faculty-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty",
      "description": "Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty 498740 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Liberal Arts Tenure-Track Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty Department Philosophy and Religious Studies University Expectation MTSU seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching, robust research/creative activity, and meaningful service. We also seek to attract culturally and academically diverse faculty who value working with diverse students. Salary The salary is commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function The College of Liberal Arts at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for the position (#127005) of Chair of the Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies. Applicants must meet the criteria for the rank of either associate professor or professor. Expedited tenure upon appointment is possible. The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will lead a department that offers a B.A., a B.S., and a minor in both Philosophy and Religious Studies. The successful candidate will emphasize collaborative leadership and the ability to manage quotidian operations while focusing on long-range plans to foster growth and sustain quality programs. In addition, the selected candidate will prioritize excellence in teaching, have a distinguished record of scholarship, and be committed to equitable student success. The successful candidate will also have demonstrated leadership abilities, strong interpersonal and problem-solving skills, an affinity for mentorship, and the ability to advocate for diverse student and faculty concerns. Required Education A terminal degree in philosophy or a closely related field is required by the appointment date. Other Desirables Applicants with prior administrative experience, including budget management, assessment, and an interest in recruitment and fundraising, may receive special consideration. Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research or creative activities (as appropriate to the discipline), and a statement of leadership philosophy (\" Other Document 1\" ) as separate attachments when submitting the online application. Special Instruction to Applicants When applying, applicants must provide complete contact information, including email addresses, for three professional references. References will be contacted to provide a reference letter if the applicant is selected for an interview. In addition, if the applicant is selected for the position, official transcripts of all degrees conferred, including translations and evaluations of international transcripts from an approved credentialing agency, will be required before a contract is issued. All submitted materials become the property of MTSU and will not be returned. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. If you need help with the application, please contact Mitzi Dunkley, Faculty Recruitment Specialist, at (615) 898-5128. If you have position-specific questions, please contact Karla Barnes at Karla.Barnes@mtsu.edu. MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: 12/02/2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 8b573c4e Last Name (required) 615c8af2 Email (required) 167628c5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Leadership, Development, and Educational Systems (Instructional Leadership), Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Education The Department of Leadership, Development, and Educational Systems at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (#115080) for its Administration and Supervision Program, including its Instructional Leadership concentration, at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. Chair, Communication Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Communications The College of Liberal Arts at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for the position (#631005) of Chair of the Department of Communication Studies. Applicants must meet the criteria for the rank of either associate professor or professor. Expedited t