    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/music-percussion-tenure-track-faculty-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Music (Percussion), Tenure-Track Faculty",
      "description": "Music (Percussion), Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Music (Percussion), Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Music (Percussion), Tenure-Track Faculty 498738 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Fine & Applied Arts Tenure-Track Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Music (Percussion), Tenure-Track Faculty School Music University Expectation MTSU seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching, robust research/creative activity, and meaningful service. We also seek to attract culturally and academically diverse faculty who value working with diverse students. Salary The salary is commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function The School of Music at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (#131130) in percussion at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be a dynamic and engaging pedagogue and performer with a proven record of excellence as a studio teacher, ensemble director, and performer. Primary teaching responsibilities will include courses and lessons on both the graduate and undergraduate level, including applied percussion, percussion ensemble, steel band, and other percussion chamber groups. The faculty member may also be asked to teach courses such as percussion methods, percussion literature and pedagogy, and other courses as needed. The selected candidate will be actively involved in recruiting percussionists and serve as the coordinator for percussion activities. In addition to teaching, the tenure-track percussion faculty member will maintain an active profile as a performer, composer, or clinician at the regional, national, or international level through recitals, master classes, and outside clinics. The MTSU School of Music serves approximately 250 undergraduate and graduate music majors pursuing Bachelor of Music, Bachelor of Arts, and Master of Music degrees, as well as many students enrolled in specialized minors. For more information, visit www.mtsu.edu/music. Required Education A terminal degree in percussion performance is required by the appointment date. Required Related Experience Three (3) years of full-time teaching at the collegiate level are required by the appointment date. Other Desirables Applicants with experience coordinating an instrumental area, professional recording experience, and working with non-traditional ensembles such as salsa bands or steel bands will receive special consideration. Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must provide the following as separate attachments when submitting the application. Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy addressing the strengths they will bring as a teacher and scholar and the ways in which their pedagogical style fits the ideals presented in the job description. Statement of research or creative activities (as appropriate to the discipline). Link(s) to two(2) 15-minute videos of percussion lessons. AND Link(s) to three (3) videos of solo performances given in the past five (5) years. This may be accomplished by providing links either in their curriculum vitae or in a document attached as \" Other Document 1 .\" The links must be active and working at the time of application submission and remain so until the search is complete. A program for a potential future recital that showcases the applicant as a performer and their strengths as an artist. The program should include 45-60 minutes of music, broken up into set groupings. This document should be submitted as \" Other Document 2 .\" Special Instruction to Applicants When applying, applicants must provide complete contact information, including email addresses, for three professional references. References will be contacted to provide a reference letter if the applicant is selected for an interview. In addition, if the applicant is selected for the position, official transcripts of all degrees conferred, including translations and evaluations of international transcripts from an approved credentialing agency, will be required before a contract is issued. All submitted materials become the property of MTSU and will not be returned. Submission of materials is the applicant’s responsibility. Applications without all required materials are incomplete and will not be considered. If you need help with the application, please contact Mitzi Dunkley, Faculty Recruitment Specialist, at (615) 898-5128. If you have position-specific questions, please contact Karla Barnes at Karla.Barnes@mtsu.edu. MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: 12/01/2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 60ca4b10 Last Name (required) 70f79e2f Email (required) 4a6cbbef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Leadership, Development, and Educational Systems (Instructional Leadership), Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Education The Department of Leadership, Development, and Educational Systems at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (#115080) for its Administration and Supervision Program, including its Instructional Leadership concentration, at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. Chair, Philosophy and Religious Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Liberal Arts The College of Liberal Arts at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for the position (#127005) of Chair of the Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies. Applicants must meet the criteria for the rank of either associate professor or professor. Expedited tenure upon appointment is possible. The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027. Chair, Communication Studies, Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Communications The College of Liberal Arts at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for the position (#631005) of Chair of the Department of Communication Studies. Applicants must meet the criteria for the rank of either associate professor or professor. Expedited tenure upon appointment is possible. The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6bd54d98 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Fine & Appli