    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/director-research-services-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Director - Research Services",
      "description": "Director - Research Services - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Director - Research Services - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Director - Research Services 498724 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Research and Sponsored Programs Administrative Job Title Director - Research Services Department Research and Sponsored Programs Salary $134,214 - $173,360; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function Reporting to the Vice Provost for Research, the Director of the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs (ORSP) provides strategic and operational leadership for the University's sponsored research enterprise. The Director is responsible for leading, managing, and continuously improving ORSP; providing high-quality service to faculty and other investigators; ensuring effective stewardship and compliance throughout the sponsored-project lifecycle; and developing the organizational capacity, systems, processes, relationships, and strategies necessary to grow and diversify the University's externally funded portfolio. Working closely with the Vice Provost for Research, academic leadership, faculty, research centers and institutes, and ORSP staff, the Director develops and executes a multiyear strategy for increasing competitive external funding from federal, state, foundation, industry, and other sources. The Director builds and manages a qualified funding-opportunity and proposal pipeline, strengthens institutional capacity for large and complex proposals, expands faculty participation in sponsored activities, cultivates relationships with sponsors and external partners, and uses data and performance metrics to guide strategy and resource allocation. The Director provides leadership across research development, pre-award administration, award negotiation and acceptance, contract and subaward administration, post-award coordination, electronic research administration, training, research compliance coordination, and related sponsored-program functions. The Director is expected to create a faculty- and customer-focused culture characterized by service, accountability, responsiveness, innovation, collaboration, sound judgment, operational excellence, and continuous improvement. Required Education Master's degree from an accredited institution. Doctoral degree desired. Required Related Experience Eight years of progressively responsible experience in sponsored programs administration, research administration, research development, or a closely related field, including a minimum of four years of progressively responsible leadership or management experience supervising professional staff or leading complex organizational operations. Desirable Related Experience Preferred qualifications include: • Ten or more years of progressively responsible sponsored-programs, research-administration, or research-development experience. • Significant leadership experience in a central research or sponsored-programs office at a research university or similarly complex research organization. • Demonstrated success increasing external funding, proposal activity, investigator participation, organizational capacity, service quality, or funding diversification. • Experience supporting or managing a significant externally funded research portfolio. • Demonstrated experience with large, interdisciplinary, multi-investigator, multi-institutional, center-scale, or strategically important proposals. • Experience developing organizational structures, managing professional teams, improving business processes, and implementing performance metrics. • Experience developing productive relationships with federal and state agencies, foundations, industry sponsors, and other external partners. • Experience with Cayuse or comparable electronic research administration systems and enterprise reporting or business-intelligence tools. • Demonstrated experience improving the effectiveness, capacity, service, or performance of a sponsored program or research organization is required. Experience should demonstrate progressively increasing responsibility for personnel, sponsored-program operations, organizational strategy, major or complex proposals, faculty or investigator support, and institutional relationships. Desirable License/Registration/Certification Active Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA), Certified Financial Research Administrator (CFRA), Project Management Professional (PMP), or comparable professional credential. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by November 13, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 20, 2026. Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 115d8d89 Last Name (required) 8d8cee9f Email (required) 594a5fed Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Coordinator - Development Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Development and Foundation Reporting to the Associate Athletic Director for Development, the primary function of this role is to secure funds for MTSU Athletics by fulfilling the interests and passions of donors to the Blue Raider Athletic Association (BRAA). The ideal candidate will accomplish this by providing prospective donors with giving opportunities and encouraging them to give, resulting in major philanthropic gifts ($25,000 and above) and significant annual fund gifts. Will also be responsible for tracking the team's major gift fundraising activities, such as monthly and quarterly solicitations, visits, and portfolio reviews. This position reports to the Associate Athletic Director/Development. It works closely with the MTSU Foundation staff and athletics leadership to execute fundraising initiatives to raise private donor support for the Build Blue campaign and MTSU Athletics. Associate Director - International Enrollment Management Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Admissions and Enrollment, International Affairs Supports Director of International Enrollment Management in all activities of the office including recruitment, admissions, and immigration. In recruitment maintains strong relationships across campus, some international travel is expected, and manages relationships with recruitment partners around the world. Assists in admission process including documentation review and processing and scholarships. Is expected to be knowledgeable about F-1 visa immigration regulations and processes for international students. Assistant Librarian - CPM Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee College of Media & Entertainment, Library The Assistant Librarian catalogs and maintains reference and research collections in multiple formats, provides specialized reference services, maintains the Reading Room, and supports collection development. The position also assists with instruction, library programming, event promotion, and daily CPM operations. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6d0607b2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research and Sponsored Programs Research and Sponsored Programs Employment Type Administrative Administrative Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) f51228cb Last Name (required) 80a5cda3 Email (required) 8f7ea607 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
