    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/associate-director-international-enrollment-management-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director - International Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Associate Director - International Enrollment Management - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Associate Director - International Enrollment Management - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director - International Enrollment Management 498728 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Admissions and Enrollment International Affairs Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Associate Director - International Enrollment Management Department International Education Salary $59,724 - $74,355; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function The Associate Director of International Enrollment Management reports to the Director of International Enrollment Management and is responsible for supporting the international admissions and recruitment activities of the university. This role is responsible for supporting the entire international admissions process and managing partnerships with international agents and Universities outside the US. The Associate Director of International Enrollment Management is responsible for supporting students through the recruitment process from inquiry to enrollment for prospective international students to achieve or exceed established recruitment goals. The Associate Director of International Enrollment Management serves as DSO and ARO to issues certificates of visa eligibility. This role supports the day-to-day operation of the office of international enrollment management. Required Education Master's, MBA or equivalent; or Bachelor's with two years of work experience Required Related Experience Two years of work experience in an educational setting Desirable Related Experience Experience with Customer Relation Management systems (CRM). Facility in a language other than English. Two years experience in international student services or enrollment field. Experience issuing certificates of visa eligibility (I-20 or DS 2019). Must be a US citizen or US permanent resident as required by federal regulations to be a designated school official (DSO) and alternate responsible officer (ARO) authorized as a signatory for student and school immigration documents. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by November 13, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 20, 2026. Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 05330e30 Last Name (required) 6216cd62 Email (required) a62cf24e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Coordinator - Development Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Development and Foundation Reporting to the Associate Athletic Director for Development, the primary function of this role is to secure funds for MTSU Athletics by fulfilling the interests and passions of donors to the Blue Raider Athletic Association (BRAA). The ideal candidate will accomplish this by providing prospective donors with giving opportunities and encouraging them to give, resulting in major philanthropic gifts ($25,000 and above) and significant annual fund gifts. Will also be responsible for tracking the team's major gift fundraising activities, such as monthly and quarterly solicitations, visits, and portfolio reviews. This position reports to the Associate Athletic Director/Development. It works closely with the MTSU Foundation staff and athletics leadership to execute fundraising initiatives to raise private donor support for the Build Blue campaign and MTSU Athletics. Director - Research Services Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Research and Sponsored Programs MTSU has substantially expanded its externally funded research enterprise and is entering its next phase of growth. The University's externally funded portfolio reached approximately $38 million in the most recent year, and the Vice Provost for Research has set a goal of $50 million annually over the next several years. The Director will work directly with the Vice Provost for Research to help build the strategy, organization, systems, faculty engagement, proposal pipeline, sponsor relationships, and operational capacity necessary to achieve that next level of performance. This position is intended for a leader who combines deep knowledge of sponsored-program administration with the ability to build organizations, develop people, improve systems, work effectively with faculty, identify opportunities, and convert institutional research capacity into competitive external funding. Reporting to the Vice Provost for Research, 