ays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by November 13, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 20, 2026. Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 4e952722 Last Name (required) a96abb7d Email (required) f3a731ed Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Coordinator - Development Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Development and Foundation Reporting to the Associate Athletic Director for Development, the primary function of this role is to secure funds for MTSU Athletics by fulfilling the interests and passions of donors to the Blue Raider Athletic Association (BRAA). The ideal candidate will accomplish this by providing prospective donors with giving opportunities and encouraging them to give, resultin