      "description": "Specialist - Graduate Student Success - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Specialist - Graduate Student Success - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Graduate Student Success 498722 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States College of Graduate Studies Other Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Specialist - Graduate Student Success Department Vice Provost Research and Dean of Graduate Studies Salary $53,954 - $66,815; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function The Graduate Student Success Specialist develops and coordinates programming, retention outreach, and student support initiatives that help graduate students remain enrolled and progress toward graduation. Reporting to the Associate Dean of the College of Graduate Studies, the specialist builds graduate student community, coordinates orientation and graduate teaching assistant training, and develops and delivers workshops and other programming with faculty and campus partners. The position identifies and follows up with students at risk of stopping out, helps students navigate barriers to continued enrollment, and serves as an initial contact for graduate student concerns. The specialist also provides administrative coordination for Grad-AI and assists with the development and assessment of graduate student success initiatives. Required Education Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution and either current enrollment in a graduate degree program or a completed graduate degree. Required Related Experience Two years of experience in student services, student programming, academic support, program administration, or a related area, including coordinating programs or events and delivering presentations, training, or workshops. Relevant graduate student experience may count toward this requirement. Desirable Related Experience Experience working with graduate students or in graduate education; 