      "title": "Early Intervention Specialist",
      "description": "Early Intervention Specialist - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Early Intervention Specialist - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Early Intervention Specialist 498723 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States College of Education Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Early Intervention Specialist Department Early Learning Program Salary $48,920 - $60,252; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function The Early Intervention (EI) Specialist will provide regular home and/or community based educational services to children birth to three years who have developmental delays or disabilities, and provide support for their families as outlined on the family's Individualized Family Service Plan (IFSP). The EI will work collaboratively with other professionals (e.g., service coordinators, therapists, interpreters, etc.) to support these children and their families by participating in IFSP meetings, completing visits together; exchanging information about strategies for helping families achieve child and family goals; maintaining accurate and up to date documentation as required by the program and by the state funding agency and performing other related tasks or special projects as assigned. Note: This position is contingent upon continued funding.contingent upon continued Grant funding. Required Education Bachelor's degree or advanced degree in one of the following: - Early Childhood Special Education (preferred) - Early Childhood Education - Child Development/Family Studies - Elementary Education - Closely related field (early intervention, deaf education or visual disabilities, special education K-12, communication disorders, speech/language pathology) or a related field. Related field means a degree in social work, nursing, psychology, education administration, or sociology. Required Related Experience One (1) year experience including practicum, internship, volunteer or work experience with young children and their families. If degree is in a related field, a minimum of one (1) year documented experience working with children with disabilities 0-5 years of age and their families. Required License/Registration/Certification Valid TN Driver's license, reliable transportation with vehicle insurance coverage required, CPR prior to or within first month of hire. Desirable Related Experience One (1) year related work experience with young children with disabilities and their families; providing home visits to families with young children; conducting and interpreting early childhood assessments preferred. Desirable License/Registration/Certification Early Childhood Special Education preferred. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by November 13, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 20, 2026. Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) cf05fec7 Last Name (required) 49be3b44 Email (required) cbaed774 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Coordinator - Development Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Development and Foundation Reporting to the Associate Athletic Director for Development, the primary function of this role is to secure funds for MTSU Athletics by fulfilling the interests and passions of donors to the Blue Raider Athletic Association (BRAA). The ideal candidate will accomplish this by providing prospective donors with giving opportunities and encouraging them to give, resulting in major philanthropic gifts ($25,000 and above) and significant annual fund gifts. Will also be responsible for tracking the team's major gift fundraising activities, such as monthly and quarterly solicitations, visits, and portfolio reviews. This position reports to the Associate Athletic Director/Development. It works closely with the MTSU Foundation staff and athletics leadership to execute fundraising initiatives to raise private donor support for the Build Blue campaign and MTSU Athletics. Director - Research Services Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Research and Sponsored Programs MTSU has substantially expanded its externally funded research enterprise and is entering its next phase of growth. The University's externally funded portfolio reached approximately $38 million in the most recent year, and the Vice Provost for Research has set a goal of $50 million annually over the next several years. The Director will work directly with the Vice Provost for Research to help build the strategy, organization, systems, faculty engagement, proposal pipeline, sponsor relationships, and operational capacity necessary to achieve that next level of performance. This position is intended for a leader who combines deep knowledge of sponsored-program administration with the ability to build organizations, develop people, improve systems, work effectively with faculty, identify opportunities, and convert institutional research capacity into competitive external funding. Reporting to the Vice Provost for Research, the Director of the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs (ORSP) provides strategic and operational leadership for the University's sponsored research enterprise. The Director is responsible for leading, managing, and continuously improving ORSP; providing high-quality service to faculty and other investigators; ensuring effective stewardship and compliance throughout the sponsored-project lifecycle; and developing the organizational capacity, systems, processes, relationships, and strategies necessary to grow and diversify the University's externally funded portfolio. Associate Director - International Enrollment Management Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Admissions and Enrollment, International Affairs Supports Director of International Enrollment Management in all activities of the office including recruitment, admissions, and immigration. In recruitment maintains strong relationships across campus, some international travel is expected, and manages relationships with recruitment partners around the world. Assists in admission process including documentation review and processing and scholarships. Is expected to be knowledgeable about F-1 visa immigration regulations and processes for international students. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 29f0d2b5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Education College of Education Employment Type Administrative Administrative Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) e7853fb0 Last Name (required) d1f9719a Email (required) 78e72d8e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
