    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/teacher-1-ann-campbell-early-learning-center-ace-search-extended-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Teacher 1 - Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE) (Search Extended)",
      "description": "Teacher 1 - Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE) (Search Extended) - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Teacher 1 - Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE) (Search Extended) - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Teacher 1 - Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE) (Search Extended) 498714 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Child Care Services College of Education Administrative Job Title Teacher 1 - Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE) Department Ann Campbell Early Learning Center Salary $48,920 - $60,252; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function Reporting to the Director of the Ann Campbell Early Learning Center (ACE), the Teacher will create developmentally appropriate learning environments and experiences for toddlers and/or preschoolers with and without developmental delays, based on individual child assessments and developmentally appropriate practices. The Teacher will collaborate with a co-teacher and other classroom adults to facilitate the learning and development of all children through active engagement in a variety of daily activities and routines. The Teacher will support families as they transition their children to and from the Center each day and will model effective practices and provide guidance and information to University students completing course requirements within the classroom. The Teacher will also perform other related duties and special projects as assigned. Required Education Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in one of the following areas: - Early Childhood Education - Early Childhood Special Education - Elementary Education - Child Development and Family Studies - A closely related field that prepares individuals to teach or work with young children, birth through age five, such as Deaf Education, Visual Disabilities, Communication Disorders, or Speech-Language Pathology. Required Related Experience Two (2) years of experience working with young children, birth through age five. Required License/Registration/Certification Active Tennessee Teaching License: -Early Childhood Education -Early Childhood Education Special Education Integrated PreK-3 -Elementary Education -Special Education Desirable Related Experience Experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: - Working with young children, birth through age five, with a variety of developmental and learning needs. - Planning and implementing developmentally appropriate curriculum and individualized learning experiences. - Conducting developmental assessments and using assessment information to guide instructional planning and individual supports. - Working collaboratively with families and other professionals to support children’s development and learning. - Participating in the Individualized Family Service Plan (IFSP) process and implementing strategies, supports, or goals identified through an IFSP or other individualized plan. - Working in a university-affiliated early childhood program, laboratory school, training site, or similar educational setting. - Mentoring, supervising, or providing guidance to college students, interns, practicum students, student employees, or volunteers in an early childhood classroom. - Collaborating with University faculty, researchers, related-service professionals, or community agencies. - Participating in early childhood program quality improvement, recognition, accreditation, licensing, or regulatory processes. Desirable License/Registration/Certification Infant/Child/Adult CPR and First Aid AED Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter, Resume, Teaching Philosophy Required Special Instruction to Applicants Please upload Teaching Philosophy as Supporting Documents section of the application MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: For best consideration, please apply by November 16, 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the position may be filled before the listed application review date of November 23, 2026. Back to search results Recommended Jobs Philosophy and Religious Studies (Philosophy), Tenure-Track Faculty Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Liberal Arts The Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for two full-time, tenure-track faculty positions (# 127080 and # 127010) at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. Coordinator - Development Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Development and Foundation Reporting to the Associate Athletic Director for Development, the primary function of this role is to secure funds for MTSU Athletics by fulfilling the interests and passions of donors to the Blue Raider Athletic Association (BRAA). The ideal candidate will accomplish this by providing prospective donors with giving opportunities and encouraging them to give, resulting in major philanthropic gifts ($25,000 and above) and significant annual fund gifts. Will also be responsible for tracking the team's major gift fundraising activities, such as monthly and quarterly solicitations, visits, and portfolio reviews. This position reports to the Associate Athletic Director/Development. It works closely with the MTSU Foundation staff and athletics leadership to execute fundraising initiatives to raise private donor support for the Build Blue campaign and MTSU Athletics. Director - Research Services Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Research and Sponsored Programs MTSU has substantially expanded its externally funded research enterprise and is entering its next phase of growth. The University's externally funded portfolio reached approximately $38 million in the most recent year, and the Vice Provost for Research has set a goal of $50 million annually over the next several years. The Director will work directly with the Vice Provost for Research to help build the strategy, organization, systems, faculty engagement, proposal pipeline, sponsor relationships, and operational capacity necessary to achieve that next level of performance. This position is intended for a leader who combines deep knowledge of sponsored-program administration with the ability to build organizations, develop people, improve systems, work effectively with faculty, identify opportunities, and convert institutional research capacity into competitive external funding. Reporting to the Vice Provost for Research, the Director of the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs (ORSP) provides strategic and operational leadership for the University's sponsored research enterprise. The Director is responsible for leading, managing, and continuously improving ORSP; providing high-quality service to faculty and other investigators; ensuring effective stewardship and compliance throughout the sponsored-project lifecycle; and developing the organizational capacity, systems, processes, relationships, and strategies necessary to grow and diversify the University's externally funded portfolio. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    }
